# ESP-IDF component selection for the ESP32-S3 BSP.
#
# The ESP-IDF package (packages/ESP-IDF-latest) ships a SConscript that only
# knows the ESP32-C3 (and, in newer forks, C6) file sets; for the S3 target it
# raises NameError because no branch defines its source list. Rather than
# patching the vendored package, the BSP declares its own esp-idf group here:
# the file list is the C3 set with every esp32c3 path renamed to its existing
# esp32s3 counterpart (checked against the package at authoring time), with
# these deliberate differences:
#   - Wi-Fi / BT / wpa / lwip / netif / vfs / nvs / esp_phy / esp_event groups:
#     not compiled (v1 console-only BSP, matching the BSP's Kconfig defaults)
#   - components/cxx, esp_pm, app_update, efuse, pthread: kept exactly as C3 so
#     IDF startup code sees the same symbol set (unused pieces drop out via
#     --gc-sections)
#   - RISC-V arch files (components/riscv/*, esp_system arch/riscv) replaced
#     by their esp_system/port/arch/xtensa counterparts plus the target-
#     independent components/xtensa interrupt plumbing, and linked against
#     xtensa/esp32s3/libxt_hal.a (xthal_save_extra_nw / window spill / cp regs)
#   - adc / sha / aes / ds / brownout-only HALs and the S3 peripheral files
#     with no RT-Thread driver behind them are left out.
#   - Left out of the xtensa arch set deliberately: esp_ipc_isr* (dual-core IPI,
#     CONFIG_ESP_SYSTEM_SINGLE_CORE_MODE makes esp_ipc.c call handlers
#     directly), expression_with_stack* (indexes the real FreeRTOS TCB, which
#     the RT-Thread wrapper does not provide), bootloader_sha/secure_boot/
#     flash_encrypt (need mbedtls / secure boot, both off), and
#     esp_hw_support/sleep_modes.c (deep sleep, needs the excluded
#     driver/touch_sensor.h; no esp_sleep API is offered by this BSP v1).
#   - Added on top of the C3 set: spi_flash/spi_flash_timing_tuning.c and
#     spi_flash/spi_flash_hpm_enable.c. The xtensa cpu_start.c/rtc_init.c call
#     spi_timing_flash_tuning() and spi_flash_enable_high_performance_mode();
#     on C3 those call sites are RISC-V-guarded out, so the C3 list has none.

import os
from building import *
from env_package import find_package_path

cwd = GetCurrentDir()
bsp_root = os.path.normpath(os.path.join(cwd, '..'))
# pkgs --update-force may place this under bsp/ESP/libraries rather than
# this BSP's packages directory.
PKG = find_package_path(bsp_root, 'ESP-IDF-latest',
                        marker='components/xtensa/esp32s3/include')

